 "kind": "lattice",
 "brief": "The base of a sensor pod on my robot's mast, printed in SLS PA12. It is a 70 x 50 x 30 mm block\n(x = -35 to 35, y = -25 to 25, z = 0 to 30) that sits flat on the mast plate, held by four M4 screws\nalong Z through it at (+/-27, +/-17): 4.5 mm holes, with 10 mm of solid round each. The sensor\nscrews onto the top with two M3 heat-set inserts at (+/-15, 0): 4.2 mm holes from z = 24 to the top.\nKeep the outside exactly as it is, with a closed skin all round (it gets dyed and must look solid),\nbut make the inside a gyroid lattice, and make sure the powder can get out. The sensor is 0.5 kg\nand the mast takes knocks of up to 30 g, so design for 150 N on the inserts, down, along X or along\nY. Safety factor 2. It is 106 g solid; get it under 55 g.",
